\begin{equation}
H(\lambda)=\begin{pmatrix}\lambda & g\\ g & -\lambda\end{pmatrix}.
\end{equation}
By Eq.~\eqref{eq:level-statistics-2x2eig} with $a=\lambda$, $d=-\lambda$, $b=g$, the levels are $\pm\sqrt{\lambda^2+g^2}$. Without coupling ($g=0$) the levels $\pm\lambda$ cross at $\lambda=0$. With any nonzero coupling they never meet: the smallest separation is $2|g|$, reached at $\lambda=0$ (Fig.~\ref{fig:level-statistics-avoided}).

